      keyLabs: ["Allergy is primarily a clinical diagnosis. Acute serum tryptase can support mast-cell activation when timed correctly, while skin testing or challenge answers protocol-specific questions; no routine blood panel proves all beta-lactam safety.", "Eosinophilia, creatinine, liver tests, CBC, and skin or organ findings help characterize delayed systemic reactions rather than simply labeling them 'rash.'"],
